description:
User feedback on 2026-10-10: "I detected some AI-isms in our frontend. First, that 'Ready to read' and 'PDF Needed' things look too verbose on the library page. I think we should indicate the availability and not availability of the PDFs but I didn't like the current way. But I liked the icon for missing PDF. Anyway, use your Impeccable design skill to find best UI/UX here. Also we need to work on the short citations here as well. Then that 'Ready to read' thing also appears inside /papers/ page."
Design (lead, impeccable skill, Operate mode; precedents: the attachment icon column in Zotero and Mendeley, and file-type icons in file managers). PDF state becomes the paper's leading file icon on every surface that lists papers: the Library, the sidebar Papers list, the @ picker and the command palette. The workspace header shows the icon only when the PDF is not ready.
Icon states:
- attached: FileText in regular ink;
- none: FileQuestion in muted ink (the icon the user liked);
- preparing: LoaderCircle, spinning unless reduced motion is set, muted;
- failed: FileWarning in destructive red.
Each icon has a tooltip on hover and focus ('PDF attached', 'No PDF yet', 'Preparing PDF…', 'PDF couldn't be read') and matching screen-reader text. There are no text badges, and the green and amber tints go, per DESIGN.md's Black-and-White rule. Library rows use PaperCitation (ARA-088): 'Subakan et al. (2021), *Venue*'.
